# Fly.io PDF worker build context (Dockerfile.worker) — this is what made the FIRST deploy attempt
# look "stuck": with no .dockerignore, the whole repo (2.1GB — .next/ build output, node_modules,
# .git history, .claude session data) got uploaded to Fly's remote builder on every single deploy.
# The worker only ever needs package.json/package-lock.json (npm ci reinstalls fresh inside the
# container, so the host's own node_modules is never used) and the actual source it imports from.
.next/
node_modules/
.git/
.claude/
public/
photographer-flow-desktop/
worktrees/
*.log
.env*.local
.vercel/
